Short:        Zune GUI toolkit for classic AmigaOS
Author:       The AROS Development Team and contributors
Uploader:     Stefan Reinauer <stefan.reinauer@coreboot.org>
Type:         util/libs
Version:      [VERSION] - Alpha 1
Architecture: m68k-amigaos
Requires:     AmigaOS 3.1+, 68000+, Installer 43+

Zune68 is a native AmigaOS 3 port of the current AROS Zune GUI toolkit.
It aims to improve compatibility with classic MUI applications while
keeping CPU and memory costs practical on ordinary 68000-based Amigas.

This alpha contains muimaster.library and the side-by-side
zunemaster.library, the Zune preferences editor, 18 optional MCC/MCP
plugins, translations, SDK headers, examples and corresponding source.
The native code builds with m68k-amigaos-gcc and requires no FPU.

Use the supplied Amiga Installer script. It shows existing and bundled
versions, asks before replacement, and preserves an existing backup.
Installing muimaster.library changes the toolkit used by MUI applications.
The plugins are loaded only when requested.

IBrowse 3.0a basic functionality is working and the browser is pretty
usable. It was tested on AmigaOS 3.2.3 with a standard A1200 setup.
XSysInfo works as well.

This is an alpha: there are many ways Zune68 can still improve, and broad
MUI application coverage needs real-world use. We need testers. Please try
your MUI applications with Zune68 and report what works and what doesn't.
See ReadMe and Compatibility for details.

Project: https://github.com/reinauer/zune68
